# Production-only overrides, applied on top of .env.local by
# `bun run deploy:backend` before exporting/deploying the backend.
# Copy this file to .env.production.local and fill in real values --
# .env.production.local itself is never committed (see .gitignore).
#
# Only list values that differ from local development here. Today that's
# just the Clerk secret key: this project's Clerk application has separate
# Development and Production instances (see docs/supabase-clerk.md), and
# .env.local intentionally holds the Development instance's secret key for
# everyday local development. Deploying straight from .env.local ships a
# backend that verifies against the wrong Clerk instance and rejects every
# real (production) session token.

# The live secret key from the Production instance's API Keys page in
# Clerk's dashboard (make sure the instance switcher is actually set to
# Production before copying it -- sk_live_...).
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=
